  "id": "genetic-linkage",
  "term": "genetic linkage",
  "definition": "Genetic linkage, in this packet’s context, means a possible shared genetic basis connecting two traits so that selection for one is associated with changes in the other. Here it refers to the observed association between intelligence-related performance and longer lifespan in flies, suggesting that some genetic factors may contribute to both.",
